WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.209 --> 00:00:02.628
Mitch Kessler my co-host
was fired today.

00:00:02.628 --> 00:00:03.545
Ahhhhhh!

00:00:04.338 --> 00:00:06.006
The network that I gave 20 years

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:07.716
of my life, is locking me out.

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:10.636
You left me in the woods
with a pack of wolves

00:00:11.053 --> 00:00:12.554
I am so mad at you.

00:00:12.554 --> 00:00:13.889
There had to be a
million and one

00:00:13.889 --> 00:00:16.183
women out there, who didn't
work on The Morning Show.

00:00:16.183 --> 00:00:18.435
I think that you're jealous
because of our history.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.312
You're not impartial
on this subject.

00:00:20.312 --> 00:00:21.521
And you're impartial?

00:00:22.272 --> 00:00:24.524
This is a good time to start
grooming some new people.

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.777
I just need to be able to
control the narrative

00:00:26.777 --> 00:00:28.487
so that I am not
written out of it.

00:00:28.487 --> 00:00:30.197
You don't have the
power anymore.

00:00:30.197 --> 00:00:31.740
We are doing this my way.

00:00:32.658 --> 00:00:35.160
My new Morning Show co-host

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.954
is Bradley Jackson.

00:00:39.748 --> 00:00:40.999
Your show sucks.

00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:42.125
Thank you.

00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:42.960
It's barely news.

00:00:43.961 --> 00:00:46.296
Was there something about
the network that made it

00:00:46.296 --> 00:00:48.006
impossible to complain?

00:00:47.965 --> 00:00:48.924
What the hell's she doing?

00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:50.801
Did you know about Mitch?

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:54.221
I'm down the road on an
investigative piece

00:00:54.221 --> 00:00:56.974
looking into the upper
levels of UBA.

00:00:57.933 --> 00:00:59.351
We didn't know, right?

00:00:59.351 --> 00:01:00.227
Right.

00:01:00.602 --> 00:01:03.063
I want you to interview
me on the show.

00:01:03.855 --> 00:01:06.191
I could give you who else knew
about what was going on.

00:01:06.358 --> 00:01:07.776
We have an opportunity here

00:01:07.776 --> 00:01:09.444
to do something
truly meaningful.

00:01:09.861 --> 00:01:10.946
This is...

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:12.322
Dramatic.

00:01:12.322 --> 00:01:13.240
Thrilling.

00:01:13.657 --> 00:01:15.701
He wants everybody,
that includes me.

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:16.994
Bradley's got to go.

00:01:16.994 --> 00:01:19.496
You and I would make a
great partnership.

00:01:19.496 --> 00:01:22.249
You have no idea how much
I've waited to hear these words.

00:01:22.249 --> 00:01:25.252
♪♪

00:01:25.502 --> 00:01:27.713
You said you have someone who
could corroborate

00:01:27.713 --> 00:01:29.381
Fred's direct complicity.

00:01:29.464 --> 00:01:31.091
It's Hannah, she's dead.

00:01:32.009 --> 00:01:33.010
Are we doing this?

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:36.638
We would like to share some
information about our network.

00:01:36.638 --> 00:01:37.639
Get everything.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:40.642
There are some really bad
things going on here.

00:01:40.642 --> 00:01:42.394
None of us are going to lie
to you anymore.

00:01:42.394 --> 00:01:44.354
We cannot accept a culture of
silen-

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:49.192
♪♪

